### MicroStore API Testing (Development Mode)
### Use VS Code REST Client or IntelliJ HTTP Client to run these requests directly.
### Ensure the backend is running via `docker compose -f compose.dev.yml up -d`

@authUrl = http://localhost:3001
@productUrl = http://localhost:3002
@orderUrl = http://localhost:3003

# ---------------------------------------------------------
# 1. AUTHENTICATION SERVICE (Port 3001)
# ---------------------------------------------------------

### Register a new user
# @name register
POST {{authUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Login to get JWT Token
# @name login
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Store the token from the login response to use in protected routes
@token = {{login.response.body.data.token}}

# ---------------------------------------------------------
# 2. PRODUCT SERVICE (Port 3002)
# ---------------------------------------------------------

### Get all products
GET {{productUrl}}/products

### Get a specific product (Replace ID with a real ID from the previous request)
@productId = a52df030-cf8a-40a8-b648-525d8f6385cf
GET {{productUrl}}/products/{{productId}}

# ---------------------------------------------------------
# 3. ORDER SERVICE (Port 3003)
# ---------------------------------------------------------

### Place an order (Requires valid product ID and Token)
POST {{orderUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ]
}

### Get user's order history
GET {{orderUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
